---
// Goal: show how to point ThinkThen at any compatible server, by address or by a named entry in the configuration file, and how to check it.
import SidePage from '../../layouts/SidePage.astro';
import Terminal from '../../components/Terminal.astro';
import Code from '../../components/Code.astro';
import { BACKEND_PAGES, BACKENDS_SEE, KEY_VARIABLE } from '../../data/catalog.mjs';
import { captioned, files } from '../../data/samples.mjs';
import { setting } from '../../lib/settings-table.mjs';
import FromYourLanguage from '../../components/FromYourLanguage.astro';

const dir = 'install/backends/system-one';
const page = BACKEND_PAGES.find((p) => p.slug === 'system-one');
const [environment, entry, badRate, plan] = captioned(dir, BACKENDS_SEE['system-one']);
const [bad, good] = files(dir);
const rate = setting('Requests a minute');
---
<SidePage pages={BACKEND_PAGES} page={{ ...page, description: 'Point ThinkThen at any compatible server, by address or by a named entry in the configuration file, and check it.' }} name="Models">
  <h1>Any compatible server</h1>
  <p class="lede">Point ThinkThen at any server that answers its questions, by address or by name. <a href="/models/other-servers/">Other servers</a> gives the request shape the server must take.</p>

  <h2>By address</h2>
  <p>Set <code>THINKTHEN_BASE_URL</code> to the server's base, or pass <code>--url</code> on one command. The key comes from <code>{KEY_VARIABLE}</code>. The model is the default unless you pass <code>--model</code>.</p>
  <Terminal run={environment} caption={environment.see} />

  <h2>By name</h2>
  <p>The configuration file can name a server under <code>backends</code>. An entry gives the server's <code>url</code>, the name of the variable that holds its key in <code>key_env</code>, and its <code>model</code>. The file never holds the key itself. Then <code>--backend NAME</code> or <code>THINKTHEN_BACKEND</code> picks the entry, and <code>backend</code> in the file makes it the default.</p>
  <Code code={good.text} file={good.name} caption={`${good.name}, the configuration file`} />
  <Terminal run={entry} caption={entry.see} />
  <p>A name uses 1 to 32 lowercase letters, digits, and hyphens, and may not reuse a built-in name. The <a href="/start/configuration/">Configuration page</a> says where the file lives.</p>

  <h2>Pace the requests</h2>
  <p>ThinkThen sets no pace of its own. <code>requests_per_minute</code> on an entry caps how many requests one process starts each minute, retries included. It takes {rate.allowed.toLowerCase()}. A built-in's entry may also hold a rate, a price pair and a profile. Its address, key, model and request shape stay fixed. An explicit profile or price pair outranks the selected setup. Setup prices outrank the top-level pair. <code>THINKTHEN_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE</code> outranks the file. The limit holds within one process. <a href="/start/settings/#requests-a-minute">Requests a minute</a> gives the rule.</p>
  <Code code={bad.text} file={bad.name} caption={`${bad.name}, a rate out of range`} />
  <Terminal run={badRate} caption={badRate.see} />

  <h2>Check the server</h2>
  <p><code>thinkthen backends check --url BASE</code> sends four fixed test questions, then one small call through each of the ten functions. It prints one row each for the connection, the key, the endpoint, the four questions, and the usage counts. Each function row reads <code>answered</code>, <code>incompatible</code> or <code>unchecked</code>. A test question's row reads <code>ok</code>, <code>warning</code> or <code>critical</code>. It exits 0 only when no row is critical. Every request is real. A hosted server may charge for it. The <a href="/models/check/">check reference</a> explains every row.</p>
  <Terminal run={plan} caption={plan.see} />
  <p>A threshold tuned on one model does not carry to another. Grade the new model on your own labeled records with <a href="/trust/">audit</a> before you trust it.</p>

  <FromYourLanguage />

  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/models/">All models</a> · <a href="/models/other-servers/">Other servers</a> · <a href="/learn/beatles-bench/#backends">Bring your own backend</a></p>
</SidePage>
